.TH SEMCTL_VALUE 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
semctl_value \- control a semaphore with an integer argument
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/sem.h>
.B int semctl_value(int id, int number, int command, int argument);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Invokes the Linux semctl syscall with an integer argument, as required by
SETVAL.  For pointer arguments use semctl.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the command result, or \-1 with errno set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR semctl (3crunch),
.BR semctl (2)
